From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:26:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: verify bridge VSI retirement

Bind deferred FDB updates to the exact PPE port membership that
accepted the event. A membership change invalidates its cookie before
the port or VLAN can publish a new one. Restrict VLAN, MDB and FDB
replay to the PPE port being offloaded or withdrawn.

Park a retired VSI with learning disabled, withdraw its ingress keys
and verify that its hardware address table is empty before allowing
reuse. Hold VSI and translation rule ownership on unverified hardware
changes. Remove both learned and static addresses for a leaving port
and update the remaining hardware multicast destinations.

Read back the complete L3 port row after its VSI binding changes.
Serialize full-row updates with L3 interface and MAC programming.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

